the SCP Foundation specializes in  tracking down and containing anomalies  that are difficult to find and that  often will do anything they can to avoid  being found one anomaly in particular  hates being seen more than anything and  will punish anyone who looks at its face  with a horrific fate  scp-096 is a mysterious creature not  only because it destroys anyone who sees  what it truly looks like no one is  entirely certain where it came from what  exactly it is or why it reacts so  violently to being perceived there are  however several theories as to the Shy  Guy's origin and none of them are  particularly cheerful some suggest an  experiment gone wrong others believe it  to be the last remaining member of an  unknown species of mountain dwelling  humanoids well one theory about  scp-096's origin stands out as  particularly tragic in nature in this  story SC p096 was not always a long  limbed pale Beast cowering in the corner  and hiding its face from the world it  was once an ordinary man like anyone you  might pass on the street he was  someone's son someone's friend a person  with hopes dreams and passions a human  being who through anomalous  circumstances Beyond his control was  made into a monster many years ago there  was a mountaineer named Jack all his  adult life he had been obsessed with  reaching higher and higher Peaks  climbing Every Mountain he could in  order to test his limits hid himself  against the power of nature and bask in  the sweet reward that was the view from  the top it began as a sport a way to  build up strength while taking in  incredible natural beauty but over time  as he conquered increasingly difficult  challenges it became an obsession like  every Obsession eventually does climbing  mountains began to take over his life  driving everything else away he  struggled to hold down a job his  marriage fell apart and his  relationships to his friends and family  became increasingly distant and strained  still he couldn't bring himself to care  much he spent his alone time in the  wilderness or every so often embarking  on trips with other Mountaineers whether  he was going at it Solo or working with  others he was living for the climb over  the years he took on cerotore in  Argentina Diego in Switzerland and  Denali in Alaska he especially enjoyed  climbing an extreme cold raving the ice  and snow as he embarked on his climbs  the few fellow Mountaineers he kept up  with gave him the nickname Jack Frost  after years of refining his craft  building his strength he set his sights  on the highest mountain in the world his  personal white whale Mount Everest  itself it was one of the deadliest  climbs in the world with its staggering  height storms and Frozen graveyard of  Fallen climbers dotting the snow always  surface but he was determined he would  not join the ranks of the Fallen but  instead be one of the Victorious that  reached the top of Everest and came back  down in one piece he could feel it in  his bones Jack arrived in Nepal with a  pack full of climbing equipment the best  boots money could buy and layers upon  layers of clothing to keep himself warm  on the journey to the summit he lowered  his goggles over his eyes summoned his  courage and prepared for the incredibly  difficult climb the cold seeped into his  core the wind snipped at his face  numbing his nose and leeching through  his gloves and boots as he went but Jack  pressed on he welcomed the sensation the  bite of it it was a reminder that he was  still here that he was still alive as  long as he could feel the pain he knew  he was alright he knew that it was when  the cold faded away turned to  paradoxical feelings of warmth and  sleepiness that a mountaineer was truly  in trouble as he navigated the harsh  mountain landscape Jack occasionally let  his eyes drift off course taking in the  sights around him he could see shocks of  blue green and red the distant bright  colors of boots jackets and hats  belonging to the Fallen climbers that  came before him those who collapse from  exhaustion who gave in to altitude  sickness or succumbed to the cold  Memento Mori he said softly to himself  these frozen bodies represented that  ever-present reminder of mortality of  death lurking just out of sight it would  not come for him though not today not on  this journey he wouldn't let it the  hours blurred together within the crunch  of the ice beneath his boots the Dig of  climbing hooks into the Earth the tug of  his trusty ropes as he ascended ever  higher Jack came to a stop there was no  next step to tank nowhere higher that he  could go he had reached the summit the  white whale was captured and Everest was  his for the very first time he was truly  on top of the world now that he had made  it to the highest point there was the  all-important task of climbing back down  at this altitude he was still in the  death zone the place where human  acclimatization was impossible this was  the tricky part the point at which even  the most experienced of climbers might  get lost in the Euphoria of the  achievement and might let their  attention slip any mistake during his  dissent any misstep could be the thing  that cost him his life there was no room  for error and no time to waste just as  Jack prepared to make his descent he saw  a figure pulling itself over the ridge  from a distance it looked like a fellow  climber he noticed the Curious lack of  equipment and the way the person seemed  to be making their way up the mountain  with nothing but their hands but perhaps  they lost their pack or left it behind  for some reason the figure was dressed  in all white from their Hood to their  boots with a large pair of Black  Mountain goggles covering what little of  their face wasn't concealed by the hood  uncertain if the figure was in need of  assistance and surprised to see another  Soul on the mountain with him jack waved  at the figure everything okay he called  there was no response but the figure  turned to look at him at least he  thought it was looking at him he  couldn't see its eyes through the  goggles but he felt the distinct  sensation of it locking its gaze with  his just the same as soon as the figure  turned to look at him jack began to feel  strange the pain the sharp sensation of  the cold that he relied on to ground  himself and remember he was really here  began to blur around the edges the  feeling softened melting away along with  the ache in his muscles the blurriness  in his eyes the dry mouth that had  nagged at him for hours he felt  unbalanced unmoored a ship with no  anchor he couldn't explain why  a sudden relief from the cold made his  chest tightened with Primal Terror he  did not feel like one man encountering  another on the mountain he felt the way  he had years ago when he came face to  face with a mountain lion staring down a  predator and remembering all of a sudden  that humans do not naturally sit at the  top of the food chain this figure this  thing it was no man it was no person  Jack prepared to continue his descent to  get away from the strange Intruder as  quickly as possible but his feet would  not obey him his eyes cannot break  contact with the figure in white that  was slowly beginning to advance toward  him one slow step at a time it was in no  hurry it knew he was not going anywhere  anytime soon he trembled as the figure  grew closer its inscrucible face hidden  beneath its hood and behind its goggles  he wished he could just see its face but  dreaded learning What secrets it was  hiding if only he could just unstick his  feet from the earth Break Free of this  spell that had fallen over him he could  Escape but no matter how much his  muscles strained how he gritted his  teeth with effort he couldn't get away  as the entity came closer the cold  snapped back into his body but something  was different it was heightened like  every icy Breeze and freezing wind  layered on top of itself hardening his  muscles to rock crystallizing the very  blood in his veins he felt as if his  fingers if he tried to wriggle them  would snap off and fall to the ground  his eyes thrummed in their sockets his  lungs stretched to hold on to each  breath as the cold constricted its fist  around his chest he opened his mouth to  speak but his voice died in his throat  coming out in a weak Whisper of air now  the thing was close enough to touch him  and whatever Force had been holding him  still and upright released him it was as  if he were a marionette to suspend it in  the air and the Puppeteer released his  strings at once he crumpled to the  snow-covered ground in a heap his cheek  pressed into the Earth his eyes trained  helplessly on the still advancing figure  his lip formed the word please though he  could not tell exactly what he was  begging for his life his freedom a  painless death perhaps he struggled to  push himself to his feet but all the  strength had gone out of his limbs he  could barely lift his arm let alone  handle the weight of his whole body the  thing shaped like a man was right above  him glowing down through those opaque  goggles he still could not see its eyes  but somehow he could feel the way it was  looking at him hatred was radiating off  of it disdain and pure unadulterated  malice then it tilted its head to the  side thoughtfully and Jack's mind was  overwhelmed with images he felt the  Phantom sensation of sunlight on his  skin and spring green grass beneath his  bare feet he could see clear as day in  his Mind's Eye a forest in the middle of  summer dewdrops sparkling on the Petals  of wildflowers blowing in a gentle sweet  Breeze then he felt sand between his  toes smelled the Sea Breeze felt the  comfort and contentment of a nap on the  beach it was not offering these things  to him but something like them something  like peace it was offering him a gift  but he didn't want it he couldn't take  it he was Jack Frost damn it he thrived  in the cold the har